; Check the CPU support the 3.2 Installer sets up, on either A3000 machine:
;   uv run amiga-env exec a3000-dev work/cpucheck/test.amigados
;   uv run amiga-env exec a3000-dev-060 work/cpucheck/test.amigados
; CPU CHECKINSTALL returns 0 when the libraries the CPU needs are in place,
; 5 (a warning) when they are missing, as the startup-sequence tests.
; CPU lists the FPU flags exec sets, so it says 68882 on a 68060 too; FPU
; (from MMULibs) names the FPU itself. MuScan prints the MMU table that
; mmu.library built, which shows the MMU is in use.
FailAt 21
CPU CHECKINSTALL
Echo "CPU CHECKINSTALL returned $RC"
CPU
FPU
MuScan
Version 680x0.library FULL
Echo "680x0.library: $RC"
Version 68030.library FULL
Echo "68030.library: $RC"
Version 68040.library FULL
Echo "68040.library: $RC"
Version 68060.library FULL
Echo "68060.library: $RC"
Version mmu.library FULL
Echo "mmu.library: $RC"
Version exec.library
Avail
List C:Assign S:Startup-sequence S:User-Startup LIBS:68060.library
Echo "Startup-sequence: " NOLINE
Version S:Startup-sequence
